/*  Choosing a value — `<value> when <condition>, otherwise <value>`, chained.

    ★ A C ternary, so only the chosen side runs, as the language promises. Both sides go in as the
      kind of the whole: the same kind when they agree, and the union of the two otherwise — each
      side wrapped into it. A side that is `void` waits (see chosen-kind).
*/

Pull books on collections, and the c-language.
    /// The kind a choice gives, from the kinds of its two sides.
    Bind text or failure to chosen-kind unto emitter, given (the node expression):
        Define taken as cast one's kind-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 1)) or pass the failure off.
        Define other as cast one's kind-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 3)) or pass the failure off.
        If taken is other, return taken.
        // One type and `void` is a voidable of it, as the checker folds it — and a voidable beside
        // its own type, or beside `void`, is that voidable.
        If taken is "voidable {other}" or (other is "void" and taken starts with "voidable "), return taken.
        If other is "voidable {taken}" or (taken is "void" and other starts with "voidable "), return other.
        Define present as other.
        If other is "void", the present becomes taken.
        If taken is "void" or other is "void":
            // ⚠ A union and `void` stays a union with a void case, `(a or b or void)`, which has no C here yet.
            If cast is-union on (present), return a failure (cast not-built on ("a choice between void and a union")).
            Define widened as "voidable {present}".
            Cast one's register-union on (widened).
            Return widened.
        Done.
        For each side in a series of text with (taken, other), repeat:
            If cast is-scalar on (side) is false and cast object-of on (side) is "" and cast is-union on (side) is false:
                Return a failure (cast not-built on ("a choice between a {taken} and a {other}")).
            Done.
        Done.
        Define union as cast union-kind-of on (a series of text with (taken, other)).
        Cast one's register-union on (union).
        Return union.
    Done.

    Bind text or failure to c-chosen unto emitter, given (the node expression):
        Define kind as cast one's chosen-kind on (expression) or pass the failure off.
        Define condition as cast one's c-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 2)) or pass the failure off.
        Define taken as cast one's c-of-as on (cast field-of on (expression, 1), kind) or pass the failure off.
        Define other as cast one's c-of-as on (cast field-of on (expression, 3), kind) or pass the failure off.
        Return "({condition} ? {taken} : {other})".
    Done.
Done.
